1. DEFINITIONS
1.1 " ERNIE," "Licensor," "we," or "us" means the applicable entity or entities within the Baidu corporate group that own intellectual property or other rights embodied in, or implicated by the use of, the Licensed Materials.
1.2 "You" or "Operator" means a natural person, legal entity, or other lawfully established organization using the Licensed Materials or Derivative Models, or exercising rights under this Agreement.
1.3 "Model" means ERNIE 5.5 Flash Base Model, limited to the specific version that Licensor expressly identifies through its official release channels as subject to this Agreement.
1.4 "Licensed Materials" means model weights, parameters, configurations, tokenizers or other processors, and accompanying code, documentation, or other materials actually provided by Licensor under this Agreement. Unreleased training code, data, inference code, or other materials do not become deliverables through this definition. Components separately identified as governed by another license remain subject to their respective licenses.
1.5 "Derivative Models" means models or adapters formed directly or indirectly from the Model through one or more of the following processes:
(a) Continued training, fine-tuning, quantization, pruning, merging, or other modification of the Model, or training adapters to adjust the Model's behavior; or
(b) Transferring knowledge or capabilities from the Model's weights, parameters, intermediate representations, or Outputs to another model through distillation, knowledge transfer, training on synthetic data, or similar methods.
Subsequent models or adapters obtained by applying any of these processes to models or adapters previously obtained through these processes are also included. Outputs themselves are not Derivative Models merely because they were generated by a model.
1.6 "Outputs" means text, images, audio, video, code, or other results generated by operating the Model or a Derivative Model.
1.7 "Annual Revenue of Related Products or Services" means the aggregate revenue recognized under applicable accounting standards by the same Operator from all related products or services that use, incorporate, or rely on the Licensed Materials or Derivative Models, during the consecutive 12 months preceding any assessment time. This amount is assessed continuously during use and is not limited to a calendar year; the same revenue is not counted twice. If a related product or service also uses other models, technologies, or components, its entire revenue is included, rather than only the portion attributable to ERNIE. Funding, valuation, and profit are not substitutes for revenue. Taxes collected on behalf of authorities are excluded, and refunds, discounts, and other revenue adjustments are reflected under applicable accounting standards. Amounts denominated in other currencies are converted to US dollars using publicly available, verifiable average exchange rates for the corresponding period, applying a consistent conversion method and retaining reasonable supporting records. For the avoidance of doubt, where the Operator is affiliated with one or more other entities, all entities under common control with the Operator shall be deemed one single entity for the purposes of calculating the Annual Revenue of Related Products or Services, and the revenue of all such entities shall be aggregated with the Operator’s without exception. For purposes of this provision, an entity is under common control with the Operator where the Operator directly or indirectly holds more than 50% of the equity interests or voting rights in such entity, or such entity and the Operator are directly or indirectly under the same control (including through common management or other similar arrangements). The parties acknowledge that the purpose of this provision is to prevent artificial fragmentation of revenue to avoid the thresholds in Section 4.
1.8 "Commercial Use" means use of the Licensed Materials or Derivative Models primarily directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation, including commercial products or services, commercially operated hosting or API services, commercial training or fine-tuning services, actual business operations, and production of content or deliverables for commercial advantage. Classification depends on the actual purpose and manner of use, not solely on whether the Operator is a for-profit organization.
1.9 "Non-Commercial Use" means use that is not Commercial Use, including academic research, education, evaluation, and personal experimentation not primarily directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation.
1.10 "Third Party" means a natural person, legal entity, or other organization other than Licensor and you.
1.11 "Territory" means all geographical areas worldwide other than the European Union, the United Kingdom and South Korea.
1.12 "Acceptable Use Policy" means the policy in Exhibit A, which forms part of this Agreement.
2. GRANT OF RIGHTS
Subject to your compliance with this Agreement and the Acceptable Use Policy in Exhibit A, Licensor grants you, solely within the Territory, a non-exclusive, non-transferable license, under intellectual property and other relevant rights that Licensor is entitled to grant and that are embodied in, or implicated by permitted use of, the Licensed Materials, to use, run, reproduce, and modify the Licensed Materials, conduct continued training and fine-tuning, create Derivative Models, and distribute or make the Licensed Materials and Derivative Models available to Third Parties under Section 3.
The non-transferability of this license does not restrict distribution expressly permitted under Section 3. Recipients may independently obtain corresponding rights by accepting and complying with this Agreement. A distributor's separate commercial authorization does not automatically cover recipients unless that written authorization expressly provides otherwise.
Uses under Sections 4.1 and 4.2 are free of model license charges. Commercial Use under Section 4.3 requires separate prior written authorization; an application or notice does not constitute that authorization. Rights not expressly granted remain with their respective rightsholders. This Agreement does not grant third-party rights that Licensor is not entitled to grant.
3. DISTRIBUTION AND ATTRIBUTION
3.1 You may distribute or make the Licensed Materials and Derivative Models available to Third Parties solely within the Territory, subject to this Agreement and the following obligations:
(a) Provide recipients with a copy of this Agreement, including Exhibit A, and retain applicable copyright, license, and other rights notices contained in the Licensed Materials.
(b) Prominently and reasonably identify modified files, either in the relevant files or in accompanying change records.
(c) If the original release includes a NOTICE file, preserve a readable copy of notices relevant to the distributed portions.
(d) Do not remove, replace, or diminish this Agreement's application to the original Licensed Materials and the rights they contain, waive recipients' licensing or attribution obligations on Licensor's behalf, or grant rights beyond those you are authorized to grant.
3.2 For any commercial product or service using the Licensed Materials or Derivative Models, you must clearly and prominently display the following exact wording in at least one readily accessible location on the relevant user interface, official website, about page, or product documentation:
Powered by ERNIE
For APIs, backend services, or model deliveries without an end-user interface, prominent display in developer, API, or delivery documentation is sufficient. Internal business use may satisfy this requirement through the internal interface or relevant internal documentation. This provision does not require branding in every individual Output.
3.3 Section 3.2 also applies to Commercial Use covered by written authorization under Section 4.3. Non-Commercial Use does not require that branding, but remains subject to applicable copyright, license, and distribution notice obligations under Section 3.1.
3.4 Each recipient must independently assess its actual use and applicable revenue under Section 1.7 to determine the commercial conditions that apply. You may establish separate license terms for your own additions, but those terms must not exclude or diminish this Agreement's application to the original Licensed Materials and related rights.
4. COMMERCIAL CONDITIONS
4.1 Non-Commercial Use.
You may use the Licensed Materials and Derivative Models for Non-Commercial Use free of charge, without a commercial-use notice or separate commercial authorization, and without this Agreement's commercial revenue threshold applying. Section 3.1 and other general provisions of this Agreement remain applicable.
4.2 Commercial Use with Annual Revenue of Related Products or Services at or below US$50 million.
Subject to this Agreement, you may use the Licensed Materials and Derivative Models commercially without a model license charge, provided that you fulfill the attribution obligations under Section 3.2 and send a one-time use notice.
For the same Operator using the same Model version commercially, only one notice is required, before the first such Commercial Use. It must identify the Operator, Model name and version, related products or services and their purposes, and valid contact information. Once the notice is sent, qualifying Commercial Use may proceed under this Agreement without awaiting Licensor's reply, acknowledgment, or approval. That notice does not constitute the written commercial authorization required under Section 4.3. Subsequent additions of products or services using that version do not require another notice under this Section, but their related revenue remains aggregated under Section 1.7. Annual Revenue of Related Products or Services exactly equal to US$50 million falls within this Section. For the avoidance of doubt, entities deemed one single entity under Section 1.7 shall be regarded as the same Operator for purposes of this notice requirement, and one joint notice is sufficient.
Send the notice to Baidu_ERNIE@baidu.com. Other than the one-time notice expressly required here, this Agreement does not require separate commercial approval for each qualifying model call, training activity, or other use under this Section.
4.3 Commercial Use with Annual Revenue of Related Products or Services above US$50 million.
(a) If Annual Revenue of Related Products or Services already exceeds US$50 million when you intend to start Commercial Use, you must obtain Licensor's separate written commercial authorization before starting that use.
(b) If revenue grows during use and will exceed US$50 million, contact Licensor in advance and obtain separate written commercial authorization before the threshold is exceeded. From the time the threshold is exceeded, affected Commercial Use lacking written authorization must be suspended until that authorization takes effect. A use notice, application, pending reply, or ongoing negotiation does not confer above-threshold commercial rights.
(c) Send commercial authorization applications to Baidu_ERNIE@baidu.com. Written authorization must identify the authorized entities, Model versions, purposes, term, and other applicable conditions. Any fees and amounts are determined by separate written agreement.
(d) Authorized Commercial Use must continue to display "Powered by ERNIE" under Section 3.2. Use lawfully conducted while Section 4.2 applied does not automatically incur retroactive license charges merely because the threshold is subsequently exceeded.
4.4 This Section applies equally to the Model and Derivative Models. Revenue must be assessed continuously under Section 1.7, and you must retain records reasonably sufficient to determine whether the threshold is exceeded. Hosting, API services, fine-tuning, product integration, and model delivery are assessed under these same conditions.
4.5 Verification. Upon Licensor’s written request, and no more than once per calendar year per Operator (or more frequently if Licensor has reasonable grounds to suspect a material breach of this Agreement), an Operator whose Annual Revenue of Related Products or Services equals or exceeds US$50 million shall: (a) provide a written compliance statement certifying that its use of the Licensed Materials and Derivative Models complies with this Agreement, including its revenue classification under Section 1.7; and (b) provide such other reasonable information as Licensor may request to verify that classification. Any information provided under this Section 4.5 shall be treated as confidential, used solely for verification purposes, and destroyed upon the earlier of the end of verification or twelve (12) months thereafter. An Operator whose Commercial Use is below the US$50 million threshold may be asked for a brief written confirmation of the applicable revenue classification, which shall not constitute a waiver of any right of Licensor.
