Licensor may revise this policy periodically. Section 9.5 governs the effective scope of any update. Defined terms retain the meanings given in the Agreement.
To support safe and fair use, you agree not to use, or permit others to use, the Model or Derivative Models to:
1. Use the Model or Derivative Models beyond the Territory.
2. Act contrary to applicable national, regional, local or international laws or regulations.
3. Cause harm to yourself or other people.
4. Repurpose or circulate Outputs to cause harm to yourself or others.
5. Defeat, remove or evade safeguards put in place by Licensor.
6. Exploit or harm minors, or attempt either activity, by any means.
7. Create or spread demonstrably false material with the aim of harming people or influencing an election.
8. Fabricate online engagement or help others do so, including through fake reviews.
9. Deliberately defame, disparage or otherwise harass people.
10. Create or circulate malicious software, including ransomware, or other material intended to damage electronic systems.
11. Produce or disclose personally identifying information to cause harm.
12. Publish or circulate generated material in a public setting without clear, prominent identification of its machine-generated origin. This includes code, posts, articles and material published through automated accounts.
13. Impersonate a person without consent, authorization or a lawful entitlement.
14. Make high-stakes automated decisions affecting personal safety, rights or wellbeing, including in law enforcement, migration, healthcare, critical-infrastructure management, product safety components, essential services, credit, employment, housing, education, social scoring or insurance.
15. Use the Model in a way that violates or disrespects another country's or region's social ethics or moral standards.
16. Carry out, facilitate, threaten, incite, plan, promote or encourage violent extremism or terrorism.
17. Intentionally discriminate against or harm people or groups on the basis of protected characteristics or categories, online or offline social behavior, or known or predicted personal or personality characteristics.
18. Deliberately exploit vulnerabilities associated with a group's age, social, physical or mental characteristics to materially distort a member's behavior in a way that causes or is likely to cause physical or psychological harm to that member or another person.
19. Apply the Model or Derivative Models to military purposes.
20. Undertake professional practice without the necessary authorization or license, including financial, legal, medical, healthcare or other professional practice.